         new SelfTest("birth_house_known", Severity.Light, "Maifailun (Nexus, 07/10/2026): Lidia, wed into the Takhi, named her father but not the house she was born into, and claimed she was born a Takhi. Finds a married character living in another house than the one they were born into and checks their family line, as the prompt gets it, names the birth house.", TestBirthHouseKnown),
         new SelfTest("tale_local_band", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 07/10/2026): a tale's last band was always looters, the weakest troop in the game. A \"local\" band is made of the bandits of the nearest hideout. Reads them for a few villages across the map and checks each finds real bandits; the log names them.", TestTaleLocalBand),
         new SelfTest("scene_surroundings_read", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 07/10/2026): a tale's scene should read differently to an Aserai in a forest at night and a Battanian at noon. Reads the ground under the player, the season, the hour and the player's people from the live game, as the scene's narrator gets them, and checks the narrator's block is written from them.", TestSceneSurroundingsRead),
         new SelfTest("scene_opener", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 21/10/2026): a conversation opened cold; Gabriel (22/10/2026): the character sets the scene by default, as captive scenes do. Reads the LIVE opening facts (LlmDialogFlow.SceneFacts) and asserts a conversation opened by the greeting gets a scene while one opened any other way (an interception, a tale meeting) does not, nor one put back from earlier today, nor one carrying the game's own dialogue, nor any with the MCM switch off (set off for a moment, restored). Then, with a model available and nothing on screen, opens a REAL conversation with a lord, starts the scene on a test greeting and plays the player speaking first: the scene is set aside, the greeting stays on screen and is the line remembered, and the call is aborted. Closes the conversation", TestSceneOpener),
         new SelfTest("scene_image_shown", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (08/10/2026): a tale's stage may carry a picture, opening by itself beside the chat when its scene opens. Writes a small picture to a temporary file, opens a scene with it through the real door (its narration refused before any model call), checks the left panel shows that very file and, in Dark Leather, that it steps aside when the chat yields to the pause menu, then closes the scene and deletes the file.", TestSceneImageShown),
         new SelfTest("intimate_acts", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (26/10/2026): 'chaque NPC avait des preferences pour certains gestes sexuels, et meme parfois des gestes qu'il n'aime pas', and 'un geste impose que le NPC n'aime pas devrait reduire le personal regard'. At Hardcore, with a lord arranged as the player's lover (regard 60, intimate; put back after) who loves oral given and dislikes anal received: the turn's reader is taught both from the real EncounterContextBuilder seam; the disliked gesture only asked for costs nothing and is learned; performed, it costs 4 personal regard and leaves a memory; performed again the same day, nothing more; the loved gesture found warms them by 1; one they are less fond of costs nothing; the Heart section names a taste only once it is learned; a profile rolled before the list widened (27/10/2026: 'd'en mettre beaucoup') is completed through the real load path, keeping what she loved and what the player learned. Skips below Hardcore", TestIntimateActs),
         new SelfTest("override_preferences", Severity.Light, "EvilPoptart1987 (Nexus, 12/11/2026): 'Changed information in character_overrides.json ... ran command cr.reload_lore ... some edits work, but preferences do not update.' With custom traits on and an entry injected at runtime that sets ONLY preferences (Polyamorous, Devoted; no traits, no kinks; character_overrides.json untouched) on a lord whose stored preferences are Reserved: the reload's own ApplyAll lays them on the STORED profile, and the path a conversation takes (UpgradeIfNeeded) lays them on a profile still carrying the old ones. Everything put back, the file reloaded", TestOverridePreferences),
         new SelfTest("override_acts", Severity.Light, "Tene21 (Nexus, 03/11/2026): 'Setting a character's tastes in the file, then running cr.reload_lore followed by cr.acts Character Name still show what I assume are the character's generated tastes.' With custom traits on and a lock injected at runtime (loves kissing and beneath, less fond dirty talk, dislikes none; character_overrides.json untouched) on a lord whose roll had kissing as less loved: the reload's own ApplyAll lays the lock on the STORED profile (what the encyclopedia reads) with kissing in one list only and the empty dislike kept empty; the path cr.acts takes (UpgradeIfNeeded) lays it on a profile still carrying the roll, and a profile of an older taste revision is not padded past the lock; the Heart line reads the authored gesture once learned; custom traits off, RestoreAll gives back the character's own roll. Everything put back, the file reloaded", TestOverrideActs),
         new SelfTest("character_voice", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (10/11/2026), after AI Influence 7.0.0: a voice of their own for every character; kurushimi00 (Nexus, 01/11/2026) heard characters recite alike. Reads YOUR VOICE as the prompt gets it for up to 40 living characters with a station, and asserts it is there, the same when read twice (nothing is saved), opens on a habit of that character's own station and age, that the habits are not all one, and that a preacher never curses. Reads only", TestCharacterVoice),
         new SelfTest("credulity", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (10/11/2026), after AI Influence 7.0.0's naivety: one rule ('to be guarded is to not be naive') served every character. Reads HOW READILY YOU BELIEVE for up to 60 living characters as the prompt gets it and asserts it is the same when read twice and is shrewd, trusting or silent; then plants a BrokenOath grudge against the player on one trusting-or-ordinary character, asserts they turn wary and say why, and takes the grudge back.", TestCredulity),
         new SelfTest("friends_with_house", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 03/11/2026): asked about the people a character had opinions on, 'they started listing names ive never seen to houses that ive never heard of'. Finds a lord whose real friends or enemies are listed, reads his RELATIONSHIPS block as the prompt gets it, and asserts every friend and enemy who belongs to a house is named with it, so the model never has to supply one. Reads only", TestFriendsWithHouse),
         new SelfTest("silver_taste", Severity.Light, "EvilPoptart1987 (Nexus, 09/11/2026): many characters loved 'silver', which only raw Silver Ore carried; the silverware is of category jewelry. Reads the game's own Silver Ore and silverware categories (ore is nothing special, silverware is jewelry), then gives a lord already met a taste for silver as an older save holds it, loved and learned, and asserts the next reading turns it into jewelry. The lord's tastes are put back", TestSilverTaste),
         new SelfTest("gift_tastes", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (27/10/2026): 'un NPC pourrait [...] preferer certains cadeaux [...] Une Dame pourrait aimer les fourrures'. With a lord already met, arranged to love furs (put back after): a fur handed over through the real give_item path (the bag-picked way) is read as furs from the item's own category, earns twice the regard its value would, is remembered as a gift after their own heart, and the player now knows the taste, which their What You Know section names. Characters met before 2.8.0 are rolled their tastes on the next reading. Picks a lord with no grudge against you; what stays behind in the save: the fur's remembered kindness and the small trust a gift builds with that lord", TestGiftTastes),
         new SelfTest("matters_most", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (27/10/2026): 'qu'est-ce qui compte le plus pour un NPC. Ses enfants? Sa richesse? Son amoureux?', and 'il faudra penser a les indiquer dans des sections de l'encyclopedia'. With a married lord (put back after): read through the real load path, what matters most to him is chosen and true of him; his page says nothing of it until he says it himself; the reserved discovery from his reply marks it learned without a free-text discovery beside it, and his What You Know section names it; an anchor whose ground is gone (a spouse he does not have) is moved at the next reading", TestMattersMost),
         new SelfTest("summoned_meeting_on_backdrop", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (26/10/2026, Rhagaea's night): the conversation a scenario's tale brings to the player opened over the game's own map conversation (the Empress in armour among her guards in the street, her vanilla greeting under the video of her bed) and the chat stayed empty until he typed. Opens the REAL summoned meeting with a lord, nothing else on screen: the chat sits on the scene's dark backdrop, no vanilla conversation runs, the character's opening line is pending (its call is aborted by the close). Then closes it: the backdrop is gone and the map is given back as it was", TestSummonedMeetingOnBackdrop),
         new SelfTest("scene_close_gives_the_map_back", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 07/10/2026): closing a tale's scene left a black screen with no way back. The close queued the backdrop's pop for the next frame, then wiped its own queue at the end. Opens a scene through the real door (its narration refused before any model call, so the log shows one [SCENE] error on purpose), closes it as the button does, runs one frame: the scene's own close must have run, what it queued must have run, and the map must be given back.", TestSceneCloseGivesTheMapBack),
         new SelfTest("scene_backdrop_suspends_the_map", Severity.Light, "Gabriel's play test (04/10/2026): closing a written tale's scene crashed the game natively; the scene had opened over the bare live map, which the hosting rule forbids. The scene's chat now sits on a pushed GameState. Opens that backdrop through the real host: the map must be suspended (a CrPanelState active, the settlement-visual tick suppressed), then given back exactly as it was, with the clock stopped. Opens no chat.", TestSceneBackdropSuspendsTheMap),
         new SelfTest("player_company", Severity.Light, "Gabriel's Invite / Request Private design (03/10/2026, after nerethi). Reads the player's real company (party, escorts, prison): never the player, every prisoner truly held, the one spoken to never offered for invitation, and a room made only of the company, seated as Invite seats them, is cleared at once. Arranges a disposable companion into the main party when nobody travels with the player (GABRIEL'S RULE, 13/10/2026), restored after via ArrangedCompanion.", TestPlayerCompany),
         new SelfTest("capture_norm_facts", Severity.Light, "Fakade (Nexus, 10/11/2026): a lady left in a garrison dungeon after a plain capture, and her realm said she was 'kept like chattel'; the garrison's lord wrote the player had 'abandoned her'. The capture line named the keeping as the offence with no fact of it. Captures a real in-party lord into the player's party, reads the REAL CaptureFactsFor over a capture event naming them, asserts still held, held in the player's party, the right sex, and that the line forbids inventing ill treatment and no longer names the keeping as the offence. Frees the captive.", TestCaptureNormFacts),
         new SelfTest("captive_notoriety", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 03/10/2026): an empress in an Aserai cell said few would trouble themselves with her. A real ruler must read as 'a ruler' whose capture is news; and when the game holds a captive of rank, her real prompt must tell her the world talks of her. Changes nothing.", TestCaptiveNotoriety),
         new SelfTest("memory_repair_accents", Severity.Light, "Shinelegacy (Nexus, 03/10/2026) and Gabriel: one command to mend every memory the console mangled before the fix. Stores a mangled memory on a real lord, as an old save holds it, runs cr.memory_repair_accents through the engine's console: the memory must read as typed. Removes it after.", TestMemoryRepairAccents),
         new SelfTest("console_accents", Severity.Light, "Shinelegacy (Nexus, 03/10/2026): accents typed into cr.memory_add / cr.memory_set came out as mojibake (the console reads UTF-8 back as Windows-1252). Sends cr.memory_add, through the engine's own console dispatch, a line mangled exactly as the console mangles it: the stored memory must read exactly as typed. Removes the memory after.", TestConsoleAccents),
         new SelfTest("extreme_trait_persona", Severity.Light, "A trait at +-2 (the game's strongest) met no persona archetype and got the generic 'figure of contradictions' line. Takes a real hero with such a trait and builds the persona the real way: the extreme must be said in it, never as relish. Stores nothing.", TestExtremeTraitPersona),
         new SelfTest("retired_persona_refreshed", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (Nexus, 02/10/2026): a companion's sister played far crueller than her traits, because three ordinary -1 traits drew the 'Sadistic' archetype. It was reworded; a save keeps the persona it stored. Gives a throwaway profile of a real lord the old wording and runs the real load upgrade: it must be derived again. Stores nothing.", TestRetiredPersonaRefreshed),
         new SelfTest("foreign_divorce", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (Nexus, 02/10/2026): a divorce another mod made (Hero.Spouse cleared) went unrecorded. Takes a real living couple and asks the daily look what it would find had another mod cleared their marriage: exactly that couple; and nothing when CR parted them itself. Records nothing.", TestForeignDivorce),
         new SelfTest("house_rebellion_memory", Severity.Light, "FloatingMammal (Nexus, 02/10/2026): a former rebel, received back, spoke as a loyalist. A rising house's members now remember it. Takes a real house of a realm, expects the members who would remember to be its adults in the world (no child, no dead, never the player) and the memory to name the realm risen against. Records nothing.", TestHouseRebellionMemory),
         new SelfTest("duel_audience", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a duel in a keep with fifteen lords logged 0 witnesses and weighed 6 as news. Finds a lord standing in a settlement with other lords or notables present, expects the duel's audience to count them (never him), capped at ten, and the news of beating him before them to outweigh a duel fought alone. Fights nothing.", TestDuelAudience),
         new SelfTest("self_esteem_climb", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): lords at 100 from chores. A lord set high (shift +60) wins a battle through the real service: the gain must shrink to almost nothing; set low (shift -60), the same win lands whole. Restores his shift exactly. Uses the MCM Self-Esteem Climb as set.", TestSelfEsteemClimb),
