         new SelfTest("wedding_day_line", Severity.Light, "fkasad (10/10/2026): a marriage CR never saw reads as years old when the couple's eldest living child is 2 or more (checked on a real lord when one exists). raphareish (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a character wed days before spoke of her spouse as if married for years. Takes a married lord, sets his wedding day to three days ago for a moment, expects his family line to call them newlyweds, then forgets the day and expects the line as before. Weds nobody.", TestWeddingDayLine),
         new SelfTest("every_verb_taught", Severity.Light, "22/10/2026: arrange_match (tashmetu's groom-side ask of 20/10/2026), reinforce_garrison, share_intel, deliver_recruits and admit_secret_lover were registered and executable but sat in no teaching list, so their own teaching never reached a prompt; each testall drove the bridge directly and passed. Reads the LIVE VerbRegistry and asserts every one of CR's own verbs is composed by a teaching list of EncounterContextBuilder or named among the verbs taught by another path (pay_for_silence inline, the violence verbs by their catalogue line). Changes nothing", TestEveryVerbTaught),
         new SelfTest("registered_match", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (Nexus, 16/10/2026): a head of house agreed in the chat to a match another mod had proposed, and nothing happened. Finds a lawful match of another house at peace, wins the bride over and the head's regard for the player (a disposable test game), registers it through the PUBLIC CrMatches.Register, checks a decider with no say is refused at the door, that the head is taught the match (and that the teaching reaches his REAL prompt, EncounterContextBuilder.Build), then settles it through the REAL bridge (arrange_match): the game weds them, CrMatches.Settled reports it, and the match is no longer pending. Restores the head's regard; the marriage stays", TestRegisteredMatch),
         new SelfTest("heart_intimacy", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (23/10/2026): at Hardcore only, the nights the player shared with a character show in Heart on both pages, sober as a diary; the prisoners the player took by force are told in the player's Misdeeds section, not under Heart ('Heart doit etre une section sur l'amour et le desir'), never what was done to the player. Arranges a companion of the other sex with two nights (a hundred days ago and today, marked [SELFTEST] and replaced on a rerun) and a lord the player took by force while a prisoner, then reads both pages through HeartPageReader and MisdeedsPageReader at Hardcore: her page counts the nights, the player's Heart names her nights and not the forced act, the player's Misdeeds tells it; at Explicit none of it shows. The adult level is put back; the nights and the record stay on the test save so the pages can be opened afterwards.", TestHeartIntimacy),
         new SelfTest("prisoner_memory", Severity.Light, "chmidt (Nexus, 23/10/2026): 'Lords and ladies should also know who I put in their dungeons, which they refuse to acknowledge if I tell them that I put an enemy lord in their own town dungeon.' Drives the real dungeon path (PrisonerMemoryBehavior.RecordLeftInDungeon, the one the game's prisoner donation calls) with a real lord and a real town held by another house: the captive keeps 'the player left me in the dungeon of X' and the head of the holding house keeps 'the player left <captive> in my dungeon at X'. The memory lines and the dungeon note are removed afterwards.", TestPrisonerMemory),
         new SelfTest("tournament_audience", Severity.Light, "chmidt (Nexus, 23/10/2026): 'the lady of Hargard couldn't even remember that I won a tournament at her city'. Records the player's tournament victory as the game does at a real town and asserts a lord of the town's realm KNOWS it through WorldEventStore.GetKnownEvents (it weighed 40 with no place or realm before, under the threshold of 50, so no one could). Then, at a town where a lord or lady of the holding house stands, drives the real audience path (TournamentMemoryFeeder.RecordAudience) and asserts she keeps 'I watched the tourney at ..., where the player took the crown'. Removes the event and the memory lines.", TestTournamentAudience),
         new SelfTest("battle_reader", Severity.Light, "chmidt (Nexus, 23/10/2026): companions forget their own part in a fight, and a lord will not believe his city was besieged, knowing only who holds it. Arranges a companion in the main party with no profile, feeds a small fight's journal (the companion felled four men and was struck down) to the real small-fights path twice: the folded line still counts both fights and ends with the companion's own part in the last. Then records a siege begun on a real town by a real lord's party: the news names the besieger, and the town's holder and a lord of the besieger's realm both KNOW it through WorldEventStore.GetKnownEvents (not merely written). The profile and the event are put back.", TestBattleReader),
         new SelfTest("combat_journal", Severity.Light, "chmidt (Nexus, 23/10/2026): companions 'can't remember the last battle you fought with them, how many kills they had or if they were downed'. Gabriel: one capture for every fight and every hero, read by a battle, a tournament or a duel reader. Feeds the real journal through its seams (a hero who felled seven men, bested one lord and was struck down by another) and reads his own part through BattleFeatReporter as a battle (cut down, bested, struck down) and as a tournament (out of the lists, no one cut down); then checks the journal's binding: a tournament's journal is never taken for a battle, a battle's never for a tournament, and each is consumed once.", TestCombatJournal),
         new SelfTest("deed_regard", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (23/10/2026): 'il faudrait que pour chaque action il y a un impact sur l'estime, qu'il soit positif ou negatif', after Arcor, whose wife the player took, was missing from 'Hold you in contempt'. Picks a lord the player never spoke to (no profile) with a living spouse, applies the deed 'took his spouse' through DeedRegardApplier (the one path every deed site calls), and checks his profile was made and his regard fell by DeedRegardPolicy's number into contempt, and his spouse's by the kin number; then a gift of 2,000 denars warms by the gift scale. Every regard is put back and a profile the test made is removed.", TestDeedRegard),
         new SelfTest("misdeeds_page", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (23/10/2026): the player's page has a Misdeeds section, 'trahisons, extortions, et tout autres gestes qui pourraient etres classes comme misdeeds', 'adultere est un misdeed'; the captive scenes at Hardcore only, the rest at every level. Arranges, on the test save, a raid and a devastation through the real listeners (another lord's leave nothing, Show Mercy leaves nothing), an adultery against a companion of the other sex, a lord prisoner handed to his enemies, robbed and taken by force, and the oath to a realm forsaken, then reads the player's page through MisdeedsPageReader with adult content Off: the adultery, the prisoner handed over, the robbery and the realm show, the act of force does not; at Hardcore it does; a character's page has no Misdeeds. The adult level is put back; the records stay on the test save.", TestMisdeedsPage),
         new SelfTest("trauma_page", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (20/10/2026): at Hardcore, a Trauma section on a character's page documents the aggressions they lived through, and never on the player's own page ('on ne decide pas a la place du joueur ce qui est traumatisant pour lui'). Arranges a companion of the player's (reused, or minted into the party) as the victim, records through the ledger the scenes use that a named captor tortured them before the player's eyes, then reads the page through the reader's seam with the MCM adult level set in turn: at Hardcore the line names the captor and the season and year; at Explicit nothing shows; the player's own page shows nothing even at Hardcore; the same aggression recorded twice is listed once; a purse the player took by force reads as the player's own deed ('oui, ajoute le vol'). Restores the adult level only: on a test save what is recorded stays, so the page can be opened afterwards (Gabriel, 20/10/2026)", TestTraumaPage),
         new SelfTest("heart_page", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (20/10/2026): love stories were kept and shown nowhere; the encyclopedia now has a Heart section on the page of a character engaged with the player, in the second person, and a recap on the player's own page. Arranges a companion of the other sex (reused, or minted into the party), gives her a profile that became the player's lover on a known day 100 days ago through the same dating helper the game's actions use, and reads the page's lines through the mixin's seam: her page says she has been the player's lover since that season and year, the date is the calendar's (today formats as CampaignTime.Now's season and year, the check that catches a wrong day base), a later night does not move it, and the player's own page lists her. She stays the player's lover: on a test save the story is kept so the pages can be opened afterwards (Gabriel, 20/10/2026)", TestHeartPage),
         new SelfTest("match_asks_the_player", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (20/10/2026): when the bride is the player's daughter or sister, the player holds the say over her hand and the door refused. Takes an unwed woman of the player's house and a lawful groom of another house at peace, registers the match through the PUBLIC CrMatches.Register with the groom's side (the head of his house, or the groom) as the decider: it is taken as asking the player, the groom's side is taught to ask for her hand, and the chat's [Y/n] names her and the groom. Settles nothing (no daughter is wed by a test); withdraws the match. When the player's house holds no unwed woman with a lawful groom, mints one into the house (no parent named) and removes her after", TestMatchAsksThePlayer),
         new SelfTest("arrange_match_quest", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): the matchmaker; Gabriel: a real marriage, her heart then her family's consent. Finds an unwed lord and a lawful match of another house at peace, issues the task through the real QuestFactory, and asks the real match check WITHOUT applying it: the law must pass, and the answer must be one of wed / not yet won over / family refuses, never a legal refusal. Weds nobody.", TestArrangeMatchQuest),
         new SelfTest("craft_weapon_quest", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 01/10/2026): 'a blacksmithing quest', the kind being part of the deal (Gabriel). Issues a craft_weapon task for a greatsword through the real QuestFactory, expects the forge key for a two-handed sword, and expects a two-handed sword the player did NOT forge (from the game's own items) to be refused at the hand-over, as a bought one would be. Moves nothing.", TestCraftWeaponQuest),
         new SelfTest("recruits_read_as_give_troops", Severity.Light, "Cost bench (09/11/2026; Gabriel: 'vas-y pour l'interprete, les refus et give_troops'): a lord taking the fresh men he had asked for was read as give_troops, which closes no task. On a lord leading a party with room, a recruit task issued through the real QuestFactory: with too few of his recruits in the player's party a give_troops stays a reinforcement; with every recruit asked in hand, DeliverRecruitsVerb.HandOverFacts and TroopHandOverReadingPolicy carry it out as deliver_recruits. Moves no troops to him; the recruits added and the task are taken back.", TestRecruitsReadAsGiveTroops),
         new SelfTest("recruit_troops_quest", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 01/10/2026): 'recruitment quests'. Finds a lord leading a party with room, issues a recruit_troops task through the real QuestFactory with an oversized ask, and expects it keyed to his own culture and clamped to the band and the room in his party. Moves no troops.", TestRecruitTroopsQuest),
         new SelfTest("scout_town_quest", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): 'Make contact with local gang leader, negotiate with him for intel.' Finds an enemy town with a gang leader for some lord at war, issues the task through the real QuestFactory, expects it bound to that town, and builds the report its gang leader would give from the town's true state: naming him and the town. Records nothing.", TestScoutTownQuest),
         new SelfTest("local_context", Severity.Light, "A local model's declared context window (fkasad, 13/10/2026: LM Studio cut CR's oversized request in its middle and the rules for a give were lost). On a real character with a CR memory, sends a long conversation through the real prompt builder to a capturing client (no model is called) with an 8,192-token window, and expects what would go out to fit, to still teach GAME ACTIONS, to keep the recap and the new line, to open the raw lines on a player's turn and to carry the compact reply budget; with no window, expects the whole conversation to go as built. Tells the player nothing and keeps nothing.", TestLocalContext),
         new SelfTest("audience_who", Severity.Light, "Who is asking for a word (Lordfadooboo, 13/10/2026: \"who is that?\" and a way to open their encyclopedia page from the invitation). Expects the popup button and its patch in place; writes the Who line for a real lord and expects their name in it; raises a real test invitation and expects it to carry that lord and show the button on the map; then starts the encyclopedia detour without opening the page, expects the invitation hidden, lets the wait run out and expects the same invitation back. Closes it at the end. Checks InformationManager.IsAnyInquiryActive FIRST (GABRIEL'S RULE, 13/10/2026) so a real pre-existing popup is never queued behind or dismissed; MANUAL only then, never for an unexplained race.", TestAudienceWho),
         new SelfTest("close_leaves_meeting", Severity.Light, "Wallace1067 (Nexus, 17/10/2026, on 2.7.12): CR never told the game a meeting was over, so its meeting menu started a battle with the party met after every chat on the road; recalling a companion while meeting his errand party left an empty battle with no way out. Drives MapEncounterClosePolicy.LeavesTheMeeting: a friendly party met leaves, a party gone leaves, an enemy at war stays on the encounter menu, a settlement visit and a briefing are not ended. Notes the live encounter facts if one is open. Changes no game state.", TestCloseLeavesMeeting),
