         new SelfTest("battle_memory_wording", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (Nexus, 13/10/2026, via cr.prompt_dump): a witness line read 'I saw you cut down 168 of them yourself at at the siege of Thorios Castle', doubling the preposition and addressing the player as 'you'. Builds the same siege place WorldEventFeeders builds and drives the REAL BattleFeatReporter the way it now wires it (the engagement noun phrase, not the already-shaped place clause), expecting exactly one 'at', no 'you', and the player named. Mutates nothing.", TestBattleMemoryWording),
         new SelfTest("realm_faces", Severity.Light, "Queens with a chosen face (Gabriel, 12/10/2026: one queen per realm, made in the character editor; CR dresses the ruler's wife). Reports the faces files read and their problems; on a real ruler's wife, dresses her in a face (the first one read, else a test face) and expects her face to be exactly that one, expects the chat to show her realm's portrait when the faces file names one (Gabriel, 12/10/2026, unless the player dropped their own), then gives it back and expects her own face and usual portrait again, then lets the daily pass dress whom it should. Changes no one for good.", TestRealmFaces),
         new SelfTest("tale_world_exits", Severity.Light, "Ways out the world takes (Gabriel, 12/10 and 18/10/2026, the Troy-inspired tale: the war ends some other way, she dies, the player weds her; one tale at a time, so a war stage nothing could leave would block every tale). A tale written into this test (never a shipped file) is taken on with a real lord; the real daily tick moves nothing while that lord lives, is unwed and at peace. Rebound to a lord of a realm at war with the player, the war is seen; rebound to a lord at peace, the war has ended and the tale ends on peace. Taken on again and rebound to a dead hero, it ends on mourning. Reads what the world exits read of the player's spouse. Abandons and forgets the tale after.", TestTaleWorldExits),
         new SelfTest("tale_companion_giver", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (18/10/2026): a road tale told by someone who rides with the player wants a companion, not the player's spouse or a child along. A tale written into this test asks role companion with with_player: a companion in the main party (arranged when none rides along) binds, and the player's spouse or a lord is refused with a line naming the companions. Forgets the tale after.", TestTaleCompanionGiver),
         new SelfTest("tale_realm", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (18/10/2026): the queens' tale is offered only in the realms whose queen has her face and pictures, and the three empires share one culture, so a tale may name its giver's realm. Two tales written into this test, twins but for the realm: among lords the twin with no realm accepts (so nothing else refuses them), a lord of the named realm still binds and a lord of another realm is refused, with a line naming both realms. Forgets both tales after.", TestTaleRealm),
         new SelfTest("tale_scenario_bridge", Severity.Light, "The tale-scenario bridge (Gabriel, 12/10/2026: a queen leaves with the player and her husband's realm answers). In a runtime of its own, fires ON_TALE for a made-up tale's ending with a real lady and her husband as roles: a rule naming the whole tale and one naming that ending both play, one naming another ending or another tale does not, the news names the husband (never '{husband}'), and PRESS_FOR_WAR between his realm and the player's applies exactly when they are two realms at peace. Declares nothing; the news it wrote is removed.", TestTaleScenarioBridge),
         new SelfTest("tale_on_enter", Severity.Heavy, "tashmetu (15/10/2026): consequences ran only at an ending, so a lady could not leave midway and be given back later in the same tale; and other mods asked to hear a tale's progress (CrTales) with what was really carried out. On a real married lady of another realm, a test tale is offered and accepted; the player's choice enters a stage whose on_enter elopes: asserts she rides with the player, CrTales.StageReached reports the stage, the flag and the elopement as Done, the tale is still under way after a day, and giving her back ends it with CrTales.Ended reporting the return as Done and her wed to him again. Restores everything.", TestTaleOnEnter),
         new SelfTest("tale_elopement", Severity.Heavy, "The Troy-inspired tale (Gabriel, 12/10/2026: she leaves with the player as a guest who may be married; her return to her husband is the condition of peace). On a real married lady of another realm: 'elope' ends her marriage, puts her in the player's party, plants her husband's StolenSpouse grudge and marks her free to marry the player; 'return_spouse' weds them again and takes her out of the party. Restores her house, takes back the grudge and the marker.", TestTaleElopement),
         new SelfTest("tale_husband", Severity.Light, "The Troy-inspired tale (Gabriel, 12/10/2026: a queen leaves with the player, her husband answers). Loads a made-up tale asking for a married giver of another realm who does not lead her house, and her husband as {husband}; binds it around a real such lady and expects her own husband bound, then around an unmarried lady and expects her refused for not being married. The tale is unloaded; nothing is offered.", TestTaleHusband),
         new SelfTest("prompt_profile", Severity.Light, "The Prompt Composer (Gabriel, 11/10/2026: \"un param MCM pourrait designer l'ordonnanceur a utiliser\"; \"mise en page par type\"). Uses a made-up profile whose default layout turns every free section off and which rewords the role anchor and (in vain) the sealed format contract, builds a real lord's prompt through the real context and builder, and asserts it is shorter than stock, carries the reworded anchor with his name filled in, and keeps the sealed contract word for word; then puts the player's real pick back and asserts the profile in use is the one it was. The made-up profile is never written to disk.", TestPromptProfile),
         new SelfTest("tutorial_gate", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo and crazyblox (Nexus, 12/10/2026): a new Story Mode game hung on the training field's loading screen; the elder brother in the party could ask for a private word as its mission opened. Asserts CR finds the game's own tutorial flag (MainStoryLine.IsPlayerInteractionRestricted) when StoryMode is loaded, and that the one initiative gate refuses exactly when the game restricts interaction. Changes nothing.", TestTutorialGate),
         new SelfTest("envoy_pacing", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 12/10/2026): eight envoys about one prisoner in half an hour, each from another lord of his realm, the same offer every time. Drives the REAL envoy bookkeeping on made-up captives: after lord A's envoy, lord B waits out the captive's spacing and may come after it, and an envoy about another prisoner waits out the quiet days after any envoy (Gabriel, 12/10/2026); once enough envoys came and left without the captive, nobody comes even a year on. Touches no hero; the made-up captive's records are forgotten.", TestEnvoyPacing),
         new SelfTest("ransom_envoy_quest", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): 'Here is 5000 denars. Bring my lad alive. You can keep the change.' Finds a captive lord held by a realm the player is at peace with, whose own lord can afford the purse; issues the task through the real QuestFactory and expects it bound to him with the purse at half again his ransom value. SKIP when no such captive exists. Pays nothing, frees nobody.", TestRansomEnvoyQuest),
         new SelfTest("prison_break_rescue", Severity.Light, "01/10/2026: the game's own prison break names the player as the one who freed the captive, but the release event does not carry it. Expects CR's prefix to be attached to EndCaptivityAction.ApplyByEscape (a game update renaming it would silently lose every prison-break rescue), the mark to answer for the marked lord only and to clear, and the rescue evidence to name the prison. Frees nobody.", TestPrisonBreakRescue),
         new SelfTest("garrison_reinforcement", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): 'Works for garrison reinforcement too.' Finds a place whose garrison is thin by the seat pack's own bands, issues a reinforce_garrison task through the real QuestFactory for its governor or holder, and expects it bound to that place with a number of men within the band and the room on its walls. SKIP when no held garrison is thin. Moves no troops, records nothing.", TestGarrisonReinforcement),
         new SelfTest("town_needs_supply", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a governor asks for what his town lacks. Reads a real town's market for the good it lacks most (twice its worth or more), issues a provide_goods task for it through the real QuestFactory for the town's holder, and expects it keyed to that good, an item of that category to count toward it, and the delivery to go to that town's market. SKIP when no held town lacks anything. Records nothing.", TestTownNeedsSupply),
         new SelfTest("plead_case_quest", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo and fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a lord asks the player to plead his case before another. Issues the task through the real QuestFactory, expects a sway AGAINST the giver and a sway toward someone else NOT to answer it, and a sway toward the giver by that person to complete it, through the same credit the bridge calls; then removes the task. Moves no regard.", TestPleadCaseQuest),
         new SelfTest("earn_regard_quest", Severity.Light, "Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a lord asks the player to win the good graces of another. Issues the task through the real QuestFactory against a living lord of another clan, expects the baseline and a goal ten beyond it, expects one point short NOT to complete it and the goal to complete it through the real regard-change credit, then removes the task. Moves no regard.", TestEarnRegardQuest),
         new SelfTest("town_food_memory", Severity.Light, "fkasad and Lordfadooboo (Nexus, 01/10/2026): a hungry town remembers who fed it and who emptied its market. Reads every town's granary as the market listener does, and words the memory a real town would keep for a relief and for hoarding: placed in that town, naming it, a deed for the relief and a disgrace for the hoarding. Records nothing.", TestTownFoodMemory),
         new SelfTest("grain_relief_destination", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): grain a lord asked for while his town goes hungry feeds the town. Empties a real town's granary for a moment, expects its holder's grain to be routed there, then puts the stores back exactly. Records nothing, moves no grain.", TestGrainReliefDestination),
         new SelfTest("private_memory_injection", Severity.Light, "tashmetu (01/10/2026): another mod injects a memory said in confidence. Injects one through the public CrNpcMemory.AddMemory with Private set on a real met character, checks it is stored private (kept to private talk) and that an unmarked one stays public. Both are removed.", TestPrivateMemoryInjection),
         new SelfTest("escaped_target", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 01/10/2026): the lord a capture task named was beaten and escaped, and the player paid the broken-word price. On a real met lord, a temporary capture task whose target was beaten: the giver's acceptance ([QUEST_COMPLETE]) settles it through the real quest path for HALF the reward, and words alone never settle one whose target was not beaten. The task, the purse, the regard and the memory are put back.", TestEscapedTarget),
         new SelfTest("interpreter_retry", Severity.Light, "Gabriel (25/10/2026), on an interpreter call that used to lose the reply's deeds with a log line only: 'reessaie une fois l'interpreteur en ajoutant un log qui le specifie'. Drives the REAL ActionInterpreterComposer.InterpretAsync with its call seam: a first call that fails then one that answers give_gold must apply the gold tag after exactly two calls; two failures apply nothing after exactly two calls (never a third); a reading with no deed is not retried (one call). No model is called; the seam is cleared after", TestInterpreterRetry),
         new SelfTest("privacy_survives_interpreter", Severity.Light, "Lufaine and Maifailun (Nexus, 30/09/2026): a character agreed to speak privately and the room stayed full. In the two-call chat the interpreter's actions replaced the scene model's, which is the one taught request_privacy. Drives the real splice (ActionInterpreterComposer.WithInterpretedTags): the character's acceptance survives an interpreter that recorded none, and a gift the scene model tagged does not. No LLM.", TestPrivacySurvivesInterpreter),
         new SelfTest("no_tasks_from_enemies", Severity.Light, "fkasad (Nexus, 29/09/2026): an enemy lord buying back a prisoner slid into demanding a deed, then into invalid-quest messages. Builds the REAL context for a lord at war with the player: it says so, and the prompt built from it teaches no task to offer and no prisoner bargain. Declares a real war via DeclareWarAction when the player is at war with no one (GABRIEL'S RULE, 13/10/2026), made peace again after; MANUAL only when no living lord's faction exists at all. No LLM, nothing stored.", TestNoTasksFromEnemies),
         new SelfTest("quests_suppressed_in_nsfw", Severity.Light, "Mechanical: build the REAL EncounterContext in NSFW mode -> SuppressQuests is true (an intimate scene never mints a quest from a vow, player report); in Roleplay it stays false (quests remain). Restores the active mode. No LLM.", TestQuestsSuppressedInNsfw),
